      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Vague UE5 proselytizing will not convince developers to switch.\n\nPerformance issues generally relate to the hugely-variable quality of user-created content and would not be magically fixed by switching engine. There is no magic fix for these problems. No other reason to switch has been given by your post beyond simple FOMO.\n\nSwitching engines would require rebuilding the entire program. This would be a *colossal* undertaking. It would also completely and irreparably break all compatibility with current worlds/avatars. That will most certainly *not* make everyone very happy.\n\nBoth Unity and Unreal are perfectly viable solutions for the sort of thing VRChat is.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
