      "value": "@{62e1338f5d95dd469bfc8f94|full_name}: Isn't there any way you would theoretically be possible to store the worlds/avatars that exist in VR Chat as of right now and move those entities into the new engine? \n\nUnreal Engine is way more efficient in everything than Unity in terms of 3D and also has a bigger graphic advantage over Unity.\n\nI'd stick to 2D when working with Unity and 3D when working with Unreal Engine especially the new changes they made to UE 5.1.1 \n\nhttps://youtu.be/FUGqzE6Je5c \n\nAll you have to recreate is connecting to a world and maybe the UI with the friends. \n\nI know it's a bit more complicated than that but I've been studying Game Design and still going for a Bachelor degree in the future for Bachelor of Arts. \n\nI worked on 2 video games before with one that was also server sided and you could join the Lobby and all VRChat really is, is the following:\n\nFriends, Worlds, Avatars at it's core and 3D Models or Worlds you can UPLOAD yourself into the game you can use a different physbone system if they switch to Unreal Engine which is way more improved and better.\n\nI don't think they would break the game if they keep the databases of the users and transfer them to the new Engine if done right.\n\nThe community is what makes it look complicated. \n\nNot the game.\n\nDon't get me wrong Unity is a great Game Programming engine but it just isn't as refined and good as Unreal Engine, maybe at some point in the future it will reach the same levels but we don't know yet.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
