  "created": "2023-02-20T05:12:30.412Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat has great potential and so does UE5 you guys should honestly give Unreal Engine a full on try even when it means you would take down the game for a couple of days just to make sure the migration happens smoothly, because without this you are leaving room for a lot of competition that can simply outstand VRChat by just using UE5, if you want to stay on top you have to make this migration happen everyone is going to be very happy about a major update like that and people would stick to the game like they used to and competition would become less of an issue since you already got a huge amount of people supporting you guys but there are already a lot of people in deeper circles getting upset about it not reaching todays standards.\n\nWithout sounding mean of course! Hope you take this as constructive criticism but Unity is simply not as great as Unreal Engine nowadays and Unreal Engine also gives room for people to actually have FUN programming.\n\nLove VRChat only want the best for the game and it's community and this would be a pretty decent and welcoming change also for overall performance reasons too you'd lag way less and it would be more optimized. \n\nSaw someone made a post but I fully stand behind Unreal Engine with this one, it's just unreal from a different dimension! ;)",
